::CW_U03_L06_GP_Q01::Passage: Talia thinks asking for critique proves she is not ready for advanced art. After her teacher explains that artists revise through feedback, Talia asks what to change first. What is Talia's changed understanding?{
~A. Artists never revise.#Incorrect. The teacher says artists revise.
~B. Asking questions proves failure.#Incorrect. The passage shows the opposite.
=C. Feedback can be part of serious growth.#Correct. Talia learns that asking for help supports improvement.
~D. Advanced art has no challenge.#Incorrect. The class is challenging.
}
::CW_U03_L06_GP_Q02::Passage: Marco thinks his father's traffic rules are about control. After his sister almost rides into the street, he understands why his father checks twice. What causes Marco's change?{
=A. He sees the safety reason behind the rule.#Correct. The near-accident changes his perspective.
~B. He forgets the rule.#Incorrect. He understands it better.
~C. His father disappears.#Incorrect. The father remains part of the conflict.
~D. The street becomes irrelevant.#Incorrect. The street creates the danger.
}
::CW_U03_L06_GP_Q03::Passage: Lena sees a cracked bowl as clutter. Her mother sees it as memory. In the new apartment, Lena places the bowl on the windowsill first. What coming-of-age change is shown?{
~A. Lena decides bowls cannot matter.#Incorrect. She gives the bowl importance.
~B. Lena refuses to move.#Incorrect. She is in the new apartment.
~C. Lena thinks windowsills are the only setting.#Incorrect. The windowsill helps show meaning.
=D. Lena begins to understand that objects can carry memory.#Correct. Her action shows a changed perspective.
}
::CW_U03_L06_GP_Q04::Passage: Nia thinks her brother's register rules are showing off. After nearly giving wrong change, she understands why he counts twice. What conflict is central?{
~A. A conflict about cooking.#Incorrect. The passage is about the store register.
=B. Different perspectives about whether careful rules are pride or responsibility.#Correct. Nia and her brother understand the rules differently at first.
~C. A conflict with no perspective change.#Incorrect. Nia changes her understanding.
~D. A conflict about weather.#Incorrect. Weather is not mentioned.
}
::CW_U03_L06_GP_Q05::Passage: Eli thinks his grandmother's stories delay chores. After finding the same street names in her old notebook, he asks her to tell the story again. What is the best explanation?{
~A. Eli still thinks the stories have no value.#Incorrect. He asks to hear the story again.
~B. Eli's grandmother stops being part of the passage.#Incorrect. Her stories are central.
=C. Eli matures by recognizing that the stories hold family history.#Correct. The notebook evidence changes his view of the stories.
~D. Eli only learns street spelling.#Incorrect. The street names reveal deeper family history.
}
